<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pontic–Caspian steppe</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pontic-Caspian steppe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pontic–Caspian steppe is the vast grassland stretching from the northern shores of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>. It was home to successive nomadic peoples and empires. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a> emerged there in the mid-seventh century following the fragmentation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-turkic-khaganate">Western Turkic Khaganate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pontic-caspian-steppe.jpg" alt="Pontic–Caspian steppe" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: YegorGeologist · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9E%D0%B1%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B8_%D0%90%D0%B7%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BE-%D0%A1%D0%B8%D0%B2%D0%B0%D1%88%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%BE_%D0%B7%D0%B0%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B5%D0%B4%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%91%D0%B8%D1%80%D1%8E%D1%87%D0%B5%D0%BC_%D0%BE%D1%81%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B5.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
